# erg-hold.ride - a flat ride for a training app to steer.
#
# The closed loop: the file states a power the rider is producing unprompted, a client asks
# for a different one over the control point, and the bike has to converge on what was asked
# rather than on what the file says. Everything else is deliberately motionless, so anything
# that moves in the stream moved because of the request.
#
# erg_lag is a second rather than the default two, because a test that waits for a flywheel
# is a test nobody runs. It is still a convergence and not a step - a step would hide every
# ERG oscillation bug there is, which is the whole reason the lag is in the format.

mode        power
resistance  12
erg_lag     1.0

t=0     watts=160  cadence=88  hr=126
t=600   watts=160  cadence=88  hr=126
